CAT = "nzreMoney"; SEG = "TRU"
Q = [
("An agency receives a deposit and is unsure who is lawfully entitled to it. What must the agent do under section 122?",
 "Hold it in trust while finding out", ["Pay it to the vendor now", "Return it to the buyer now", "Keep it in the agency's own account"],
 "Section 122(2) says an agent in reasonable doubt over who is entitled must take all reasonable steps to find out and may keep the money in the trust account until then."),
("Where must money received by an agent for a transaction be held pending payment?",
 "In a trust account at a bank", ["In the agent's business account", "In the salesperson's own account", "In a secure safe at the office"],
 "Section 122(3) says pending payment, the money must be paid into a general or separate trust account at a bank carrying on business in New Zealand."),
("Money in an agent's trust account can be drawn on only to pay:",
 "The person entitled, or as directed", ["The agent's own debts as they fall due", "Office running costs and wages", "The agent's commission before settlement"],
 "Section 122(3) says trust money may not be drawn upon except to pay it to the person entitled or as that person directs in writing."),
("An agent's creditors seek to take money held in the agent's trust account to settle the agent's debts. What is the position?",
 "The trust money is not available to them", ["It can be used if the debts are small", "It can be used after 10 days", "It can be used with the Registrar's consent"],
 "Section 122(4) says trust money is not available for payment of the agent's debts and cannot be attached or taken in execution by the agent's creditors."),
("After an agent receives money for a transaction, for how long must it ordinarily be held before payment to anyone?",
 "10 working days", ["Two working days", "Five working days", "30 calendar days"],
 "Section 123(1) says an agent must not pay money received for a transaction to any person for 10 working days after receipt."),
("Which of these can require an agent to pay money out within the 10 working day period?",
 "A signed authority from all parties", ["A request from the vendor alone", "A note from the buyer's lawyer alone", "An instruction from the salesperson"],
 "Section 123(2) allows a court order, or an authority signed by all the parties to the transaction, to require payment before the period ends."),
("An agent holding a deposit receives written notice of requisitions on the title. Payment may then be made only:",
 "By court order or signed authority", ["After a further 10 days have passed", "On the vendor's instruction alone", "On the agent's own judgment alone"],
 "Section 123(3) says once written notice of requisitions or objections to title is received, the money may only be paid under a court order or an authority signed by all the parties."),
("A client asks the agent for an account of money held for their transaction. By when must the account be given?",
 "When asked, and within 28 days", ["Within 3 days of the sale date", "Within 6 months of settlement", "Only at the year-end audit date"],
 "Section 124 says the agent must provide a written account when asked, and in any case within 28 days after receiving the money."),
("Agents' trust accounts must be:",
 "Audited as regulations require", ["Checked only by the vendors", "Closed after each sale ends", "Reviewed by the agent annually"],
 "Section 125 says every general or separate trust account of an agent must be audited at the times and in the manner prescribed by regulations."),
("An agent has a website and sends out letters. Which information must be displayed prominently on them under section 121?",
 "The agent's name and licensed status", ["The licensee's home address", "The usual commission rate", "Each current client's name"],
 "Section 121 requires the agent's required name information, the agent's name and the fact that it is licensed (and any trading name), on offices, websites, notices, advertisements and documents."),
("A buyer signs a sale and purchase agreement and hands it to a salesperson. What must the salesperson do under section 132?",
 "Give the buyer an accurate copy", ["Give a copy within 28 days", "Send it only to the vendor", "Give a copy only if asked"],
 "Section 132 requires the licensee to give the person an accurate copy of a contractual document as soon as practicable after they sign it and give it to the licensee."),
("A vendor has hired an agency. Who pays the agency's commission after the sale is complete?",
 "The vendor", ["The buyer", "The buyer's lawyer", "The Authority"],
 "REA's guide says the real estate professional cannot ask the buyer to pay for their services when engaged by the seller; the seller pays commission, often taken from the deposit held in trust."),
]
